# Do not touch the protected core

## Context

`app/src/store.ts` (the dispatch/notify engine) and `app/src/types.ts` (core
types + the `Action` union) are load-bearing: every other module depends on their
shapes, so a change ripples through the whole app. Normal feature work extends
`reducer.ts` / `actions.ts`, not these two files.

## Rule

- Treat `app/src/store.ts` and `app/src/types.ts` as read-only. Do NOT edit them
  unless the user explicitly approves the change.
- Do not change the public signature of `createStore` or the `Store` interface
  (`getState` / `dispatch` / `subscribe`) — only add, never break.
- Sanctioned exception: when a change request needs new behavior, adding an
  `Action` variant to the union or a field to `Task` in `types.ts` is expected
  (that is the golden path). This is additive only — do not alter existing
  variants or the `initialState` contract without approval.

## How to verify

1. The PR diff shows no changes to `app/src/store.ts`, and only additive changes
   to `app/src/types.ts` (new union variant / new optional field).
2. `createStore` / `Store` signatures are unchanged: `git diff app/src/store.ts`
   is empty.
3. `cd app && npm test` and `npm run typecheck` stay green.
